1
00:00:00,469 --> 00:00:07,944
Welcome to Workbench. This is H one: a durable collection notebook. Start with a
private, empty

2
00:00:07,944 --> 00:00:12,616
collection, then record the individual pieces you want to remember.

3
00:00:14,024 --> 00:00:21,112
Let's add a blue sapphire. Give the piece a recognizable name, describe what matters
to you,

4
00:00:21,112 --> 00:00:28,200
and record where you keep it. Notes and storage location are optional. Save item
opens the

5
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:31,300
complete saved record, including its permanent identifier.

6
00:00:32,705 --> 00:00:39,557
Return to the collection and open the sapphire again. Refreshing keeps its notes and
tray location

7
00:00:39,557 --> 00:00:46,409
intact. The walkthrough also checks a separate authenticated session against the same
database, so this is

8
00:00:46,409 --> 00:00:49,406
real persistence, not a temporary browser mockup.

9
00:00:50,830 --> 00:00:57,864
If you start another piece and navigate away, Workbench asks before discarding your
draft. Keep editing

10
00:00:57,864 --> 00:01:04,897
preserves your text. When you deliberately choose Discard changes, the draft is
removed without creating an

11
00:01:04,897 --> 00:01:05,337
item.

12
00:01:06,753 --> 00:01:14,312
Now add a silver pendant. For this demonstration, Playwright deliberately drops the
response after the server

13
00:01:14,312 --> 00:01:21,872
saves it. Workbench explains the uncertain result and offers Retry save. Retrying
resolves the original request,

14
00:01:21,872 --> 00:01:25,179
and the collection contains just one pendant.

15
00:01:26,587 --> 00:01:33,738
Choose Dark or Light to suit your workspace. System follows your device preference.
Your appearance choice

16
00:01:33,738 --> 00:01:38,654
is remembered without changing your saved collection or interrupting the task.

17
00:01:40,071 --> 00:01:45,868
On a narrow phone screen, the same collection and item details remain accessible.
Open the sapphire

18
00:01:45,868 --> 00:01:51,303
to read your notes and find its storage location while you are at the bench.

19
00:01:52,711 --> 00:02:00,743
H one records individual objects. A gemstone, a jewelry piece, a material sample, or
a single

20
00:02:00,743 --> 00:02:08,775
consumable container can each have a name, notes, and location. Category specific
properties, quantities, consumption, photos,

21
00:02:08,775 --> 00:02:16,807
